{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f...65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f...65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309","permalink_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/OmniNode-ai:4bc2437...OmniNode-ai:65c237c","diff_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f...65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/compare/4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f...65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309.patch","base_commit":{"sha":"4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f","node_id":"C_kwDOR6jjtdoAKDRiYzI0MzcyMTA5Mzk3MDJmYTBkYzg1MjkzNjJjMGE3YzIzMTA0OWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jonah Gray","email":"jonah@omninode.ai","date":"2026-09-14T09:11:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-09-14T09:11:34Z"},"message":"fix(OMN-18332): transcribe criterion bindings on the born mint path too (#2537)\n\n* fix(OMN-18332): transcribe criterion bindings on the born mint path too\n\nAC6. The transcription landed on one of the two producers that mint OCC\nevidence companions and was proven there; the other one, which mints the\nmajority, had no Linear read at all.\n\nMeasured on the deployed effects container between its 2026-09-14T03:38:44Z\nrestart and 06:1xZ: nine companions minted, seven carrying\n`runner: node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect` (the born path) and two carrying\n`runner: node_occ_companion_compute`, and not one of the nine carrying a\nbinds_ac key. Positive control: 65 contracts on OCC dev do carry one. The\ndeployed emitter contains zero occurrences of the string `ac_bindings` while\nthe renderer that would emit it sits unused in the emitter's own package.\n\nThe two compute-path companions are correct as minted: probed live through the\nruntime's own key, OMN-18033 and OMN-13912 declare no falsifiers and yield zero\nbindings. The born-path ones are not: OMN-18333 yields five bindings, four of\nthem accepted, from the same reader, and its companion claimed none of them.\n\nThe read now lives in one module, `omnimarket.occ_ticket_bindings`, imported by\nboth producers, so wiring it to one and missing the other is a deliberate act\nrather than the default. `render_companion_contract` and\n`render_downstream_dod_evidence_item` take `ac_bindings` and render it on the\ndownstream item exactly where the compute twin renders it; the F-04 repair path\ntakes the same records, so a second companion on a shared ticket cannot bind\nwhere the first one did not. Empty renders bytes identical to today, so a\nLinear outage or a ticket that declared no falsifiers costs the bindings and\nnever the mint.\n\nRED first: nine tests failed against the unwired tree, nine pass now. 964\npassed / 12 skipped across the four affected node suites plus the occ unit\nsuite; mypy --strict and pre-commit clean.\n\n* fix(OMN-18332): home the shared reader inside the effect that owns the transport\n\nThe first commit put the shared Linear read at `src/omnimarket/occ_ticket_bindings.py`,\nwhich the imperative-contract guard correctly refused: a raw HTTP call from a\nfreestanding `src/` module is exactly the violation it blocks (OMN-12515). Verified\nby running the guard locally against this worktree -- exit 1 naming\n`occ_ticket_bindings.py: hybrid (live)` at the urlopen line, exit 0 with no blocking\nsection after the move, same command, same allowlists, no allowlist entry added.\n\nThe module now sits beside `occ_evidence_stamp.py` in the born-path effect's\nhandlers package, which is where the OCC authoring helpers already live and where\n`node_occ_companion_compute` already imports them from -- so the read follows the\ncross-node dependency direction that exists rather than adding a second one, and\nthe transport sits inside an EFFECT where it belongs.\n\n964 passed / 12 skipped across the four affected node suites plus the occ unit\nsuite; mypy --strict and pre-commit clean.","tree":{"sha":"ee6d60a49e1f71bcb7da1cb5efa5f42f3928aa2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/trees/ee6d60a49e1f71bcb7da1cb5efa5f42f3928aa2c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/commits/4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp7pGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGiEQABhDIzycve6/yRUskBicfr8r\nCFa0zcycggh9/0ZJU/e2AiTzFFV21dLYCBDDggkNFfl4AuB0Hvb9xk6oJEHJO6lU\nfNJsJmtaypzQlWFqDrtGsE9N0ODOE/Eft5p1Qb0RdVa68+3QuKwSlgESDb9Tsrbg\nJp0XaS+13XEt/hEXtv76s471PZpqemakOH1qs0mZgKwPYiIRfoLyN7S28Zutt7ho\nMU6//6Wrt9ZCGQvlrXCy5eowKgM9rzFXKyX3OXxH0h7XIsTajinlkXdvVGgxX1bS\nohnZvrC5GXrPCTbs3oq0DhQM7jh7se8ECe0AOexqdhf8Q/HHukonHMtKI0dKnCPF\nqXx+IDekdv5vu+yaU5i9CDZfB48BtID9VYdqVDBGIgE8LeEcWiThI9r3ApXVyfPl\nsv2yUdOJAFljU1hi9nDuHCW34CFuD9qVaVQV0KqgMcmpUCsucRGD/VBTyqugud6d\nmWer5R9yxxP0gkdQzLVCgVnud2dsN8HMO4rdDmshBOZGpI8G4T8zs1nbmdsEm0al\nIg720BE40OoTWui0vA58vR+ur+L1TqljDwDRzuS0FDmoWWUellY2r8Wp191/487z\nt5s0PAeZEs8yuKxBMI/pFjSWIW9ibAiH/W7xqMI3yo0FQfwPI36/W3ijTBzi8Krp\nM1nHhgSgTcI6KWyQiKjF\n=QxWs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ee6d60a49e1f71bcb7da1cb5efa5f42f3928aa2c\nparent 65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309\nauthor Jonah Gray <jonah@omninode.ai> 1789377094 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789377094 +0000\n\nfix(OMN-18332): transcribe criterion bindings on the born mint path too (#2537)\n\n* fix(OMN-18332): transcribe criterion bindings on the born mint path too\n\nAC6. The transcription landed on one of the two producers that mint OCC\nevidence companions and was proven there; the other one, which mints the\nmajority, had no Linear read at all.\n\nMeasured on the deployed effects container between its 2026-09-14T03:38:44Z\nrestart and 06:1xZ: nine companions minted, seven carrying\n`runner: node_pr_lifecycle_fix_effect` (the born path) and two carrying\n`runner: node_occ_companion_compute`, and not one of the nine carrying a\nbinds_ac key. Positive control: 65 contracts on OCC dev do carry one. The\ndeployed emitter contains zero occurrences of the string `ac_bindings` while\nthe renderer that would emit it sits unused in the emitter's own package.\n\nThe two compute-path companions are correct as minted: probed live through the\nruntime's own key, OMN-18033 and OMN-13912 declare no falsifiers and yield zero\nbindings. The born-path ones are not: OMN-18333 yields five bindings, four of\nthem accepted, from the same reader, and its companion claimed none of them.\n\nThe read now lives in one module, `omnimarket.occ_ticket_bindings`, imported by\nboth producers, so wiring it to one and missing the other is a deliberate act\nrather than the default. `render_companion_contract` and\n`render_downstream_dod_evidence_item` take `ac_bindings` and render it on the\ndownstream item exactly where the compute twin renders it; the F-04 repair path\ntakes the same records, so a second companion on a shared ticket cannot bind\nwhere the first one did not. Empty renders bytes identical to today, so a\nLinear outage or a ticket that declared no falsifiers costs the bindings and\nnever the mint.\n\nRED first: nine tests failed against the unwired tree, nine pass now. 964\npassed / 12 skipped across the four affected node suites plus the occ unit\nsuite; mypy --strict and pre-commit clean.\n\n* fix(OMN-18332): home the shared reader inside the effect that owns the transport\n\nThe first commit put the shared Linear read at `src/omnimarket/occ_ticket_bindings.py`,\nwhich the imperative-contract guard correctly refused: a raw HTTP call from a\nfreestanding `src/` module is exactly the violation it blocks (OMN-12515). Verified\nby running the guard locally against this worktree -- exit 1 naming\n`occ_ticket_bindings.py: hybrid (live)` at the urlopen line, exit 0 with no blocking\nsection after the move, same command, same allowlists, no allowlist entry added.\n\nThe module now sits beside `occ_evidence_stamp.py` in the born-path effect's\nhandlers package, which is where the OCC authoring helpers already live and where\n`node_occ_companion_compute` already imports them from -- so the read follows the\ncross-node dependency direction that exists rather than adding a second one, and\nthe transport sits inside an EFFECT where it belongs.\n\n964 passed / 12 skipped across the four affected node suites plus the occ unit\nsuite; mypy --strict and pre-commit clean.","verified_at":"2026-09-14T09:11:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/4bc2437210939702fa0dc8529362c0a7c231049f/comments","author":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309"}]},"merge_base_commit":{"sha":"65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309","node_id":"C_kwDOR6jjtdoAKDY1YzIzN2NkYzkxNGE2YzdjMWUxNWRlMzA4OTg2ZWM2NWMyNGYzMDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jonah Gray","email":"jonah@omninode.ai","date":"2026-09-14T07:53:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-09-14T07:53:56Z"},"message":"fix(OMN-18349): feed the golden corpus at the rate the lane actually serves (#2538)\n\nThe first nightly run that reached the lane (34810939133) published all nine\ncases at once under one deadline, on a comment reading \"the platform is expected\nto serve them concurrently\". It is not, and three declarations already said so:\n\n  * the delegate-skill command consumer's poll loop is serial -- it awaits each\n    dispatch before requesting the next record;\n  * the tier every case enters on is one physical endpoint permitting one\n    running generation;\n  * a handler that hits its execution budget stops WAITING for its delegation,\n    it does not stop the delegation, so each abandoned workflow went on\n    competing for that single slot.\n\nMeasured on that run's own projection rows: cases three through seven were each\ncancelled at an exact 240.000s cadence -- 06:00:37.87, 06:04:37.88, 06:08:37.88,\n06:12:37.89, 06:16:37.89 -- every one having spent its whole budget behind work\nthe probe had already given up on.\n\nThe per-case deadline was also taken from the wrong contract:\nnode_delegation_orchestrator's completion_bound (900s), a real bound for a node\nthat does not serve this probe. The node that does is\nnode_delegate_skill_orchestrator, whose handler_execution_budget (240s,\nOMN-15504) is what terminalises a case. 660 of those 900 seconds were spent\nwaiting for an event the platform had already decided not to produce. That the\ntwo declared bounds disagree is a real finding and is NOT resolved here.\n\nAnd the empty rows those cancellations produce were being reported as the wrong\ndefect. delegation_events carries no terminal_state and no status column, so\nrow_terminal defaulted every row to \"completed\" and a cancelled delegation was\nscored against the completed-row expectations as \"tokens: expected positive, got\ninput=0 output=0\" -- a description of the OMN-13535 telemetry-drop regression,\nwhich was not happening. Five of nine cases were misreported that way.\n\nChanges:\n  * the corpus is published in waves sized to the entry tier's declared\n    max_concurrent_generations, each wave drained before the next is published;\n  * that number is now a field on the saturation policy rather than a sentence\n    in its header, and an undeclared one RAISES rather than defaulting;\n  * the per-case deadline reads the handler execution budget of the node that\n    serves the probe;\n  * a budget-timeout row is classified as terminal \"timeout\" and reported as a\n    named delegation timeout quoting the budget;\n  * delegation_events is an upsert, so a budget-timeout row is given the\n    declared projection margin to be superseded -- correlation id 0df23c72\n    projected empty at 05:56:37.886Z and the real terminal, 77/1819 tokens and\n    the gate passed, landed 12.9 seconds later over the top of it;\n  * timeout-minutes goes 45 -> 70, and scripts/ci/check_nightly_corpus_budget.py\n    recomputes the ceiling from the corpus, the contract and the overlay using\n    the probe's own arithmetic and fails if the budget is below it -- a job\n    cancelled mid-corpus skips its if: always() uploads and leaves a red night\n    with no scoreboard, which is AC3 failing by another route.\n\nWired as the nightly-corpus-budget pre-commit hook AND\ntests/test_delegation_nightly_budget.py inside the required pytest job, same\npredicate both sides.\n\nFalsification controls run, each restored byte-identical afterwards: restoring\nthe fan-out publish turns the interleave test RED at \"assert 9 <= 1\"; restoring\nthe old terminal default reproduces the live misreport string verbatim;\nremoving the supersession window returns the stale empty row; restoring the\nother node's completion bound turns both deadline tests RED and drives the\nderived ceiling from 59 to 158 minutes. Committed positive controls cover an\nundeclared concurrency, an ordinary row still reading \"completed\", a never-\nsuperseded row, and a budget above the ceiling.\n\npre-commit run --all-files exit 0 across 92 hooks, mypy src/ --strict clean.","tree":{"sha":"856a43d8274b3fca5dab7cc24963b38b38db2b52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/trees/856a43d8274b3fca5dab7cc24963b38b38db2b52"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/git/commits/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp6gUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAC+4QABz8ViaTlObPhmyOnrT/JzmC\nXByl2hlmh0UrmJjWNVEEXZxwMf/3KEO0v++L97Ra17zN5V9G3BuXzo33ojc0jNIs\nbhLQkf1+7G2dropRwSLTMmrCbSGOZlyq/eIxb1w8/nMhQhr+ESp92ICfw7ySTVqo\n6A6gCsqwitJa0sShrxYH3TozCp62a+lBKxILjrwSfSJhm4JXeqGp+ARX314a4XR2\nE5MuYxUu8zAVz4MraHumBt+qJVJThP+7Jvv3U8KJHj+7nNRwhFL+kXDnlh0wPdIx\ntqDpj0C2EJd7Uc52bK46EjYueQSTTRW60cD3cBWCaHJUt2q4WWpeYcf+Vm83TBzY\nT5ih5fCBCO6EHXTX6Qg859XmXkDIvQM6DtG0KSC/LxuVX8t0MLgTQrHGcewpwZzr\n+/eor5DTDTZccyA7MRHQSu4uLwr+ckcMLL61XFpyUdYzv/NiR8QNl7YgX9O2a3uu\nTb9I4jXzchznJYyPbCbwrmhR5kFKXuFXclYYeVgeQamcUKG0dNX6bltwuN95JbZJ\nRNM4m69kW8elB1JA6HZzcBpBQNV1nFBoCt4pm3th/yJ+IM5uNAlPkcFRUNyb7QAH\nBdyHWphD5e/lQIsKDu3T9Z810E1kBSO4ARfT07obWQCc8VhJoVNATPFp12MJFABz\nx8YyMpz9Zq3p4ddObYhB\n=ZM9r\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 856a43d8274b3fca5dab7cc24963b38b38db2b52\nparent 1b5a6c4b6061804140fe1582061f345e0f973937\nauthor Jonah Gray <jonah@omninode.ai> 1789372436 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789372436 +0000\n\nfix(OMN-18349): feed the golden corpus at the rate the lane actually serves (#2538)\n\nThe first nightly run that reached the lane (34810939133) published all nine\ncases at once under one deadline, on a comment reading \"the platform is expected\nto serve them concurrently\". It is not, and three declarations already said so:\n\n  * the delegate-skill command consumer's poll loop is serial -- it awaits each\n    dispatch before requesting the next record;\n  * the tier every case enters on is one physical endpoint permitting one\n    running generation;\n  * a handler that hits its execution budget stops WAITING for its delegation,\n    it does not stop the delegation, so each abandoned workflow went on\n    competing for that single slot.\n\nMeasured on that run's own projection rows: cases three through seven were each\ncancelled at an exact 240.000s cadence -- 06:00:37.87, 06:04:37.88, 06:08:37.88,\n06:12:37.89, 06:16:37.89 -- every one having spent its whole budget behind work\nthe probe had already given up on.\n\nThe per-case deadline was also taken from the wrong contract:\nnode_delegation_orchestrator's completion_bound (900s), a real bound for a node\nthat does not serve this probe. The node that does is\nnode_delegate_skill_orchestrator, whose handler_execution_budget (240s,\nOMN-15504) is what terminalises a case. 660 of those 900 seconds were spent\nwaiting for an event the platform had already decided not to produce. That the\ntwo declared bounds disagree is a real finding and is NOT resolved here.\n\nAnd the empty rows those cancellations produce were being reported as the wrong\ndefect. delegation_events carries no terminal_state and no status column, so\nrow_terminal defaulted every row to \"completed\" and a cancelled delegation was\nscored against the completed-row expectations as \"tokens: expected positive, got\ninput=0 output=0\" -- a description of the OMN-13535 telemetry-drop regression,\nwhich was not happening. Five of nine cases were misreported that way.\n\nChanges:\n  * the corpus is published in waves sized to the entry tier's declared\n    max_concurrent_generations, each wave drained before the next is published;\n  * that number is now a field on the saturation policy rather than a sentence\n    in its header, and an undeclared one RAISES rather than defaulting;\n  * the per-case deadline reads the handler execution budget of the node that\n    serves the probe;\n  * a budget-timeout row is classified as terminal \"timeout\" and reported as a\n    named delegation timeout quoting the budget;\n  * delegation_events is an upsert, so a budget-timeout row is given the\n    declared projection margin to be superseded -- correlation id 0df23c72\n    projected empty at 05:56:37.886Z and the real terminal, 77/1819 tokens and\n    the gate passed, landed 12.9 seconds later over the top of it;\n  * timeout-minutes goes 45 -> 70, and scripts/ci/check_nightly_corpus_budget.py\n    recomputes the ceiling from the corpus, the contract and the overlay using\n    the probe's own arithmetic and fails if the budget is below it -- a job\n    cancelled mid-corpus skips its if: always() uploads and leaves a red night\n    with no scoreboard, which is AC3 failing by another route.\n\nWired as the nightly-corpus-budget pre-commit hook AND\ntests/test_delegation_nightly_budget.py inside the required pytest job, same\npredicate both sides.\n\nFalsification controls run, each restored byte-identical afterwards: restoring\nthe fan-out publish turns the interleave test RED at \"assert 9 <= 1\"; restoring\nthe old terminal default reproduces the live misreport string verbatim;\nremoving the supersession window returns the stale empty row; restoring the\nother node's completion bound turns both deadline tests RED and drives the\nderived ceiling from 59 to 158 minutes. Committed positive controls cover an\nundeclared concurrency, an ordinary row still reading \"completed\", a never-\nsuperseded row, and a budget above the ceiling.\n\npre-commit run --all-files exit 0 across 92 hooks, mypy src/ --strict clean.","verified_at":"2026-09-14T07:53:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/65c237cdc914a6c7c1e15de308986ec65c24f309/comments","author":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1b5a6c4b6061804140fe1582061f345e0f973937","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commits/1b5a6c4b6061804140fe1582061f345e0f973937","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnimarket/commit/1b5a6c4b6061804140fe1582061f345e0f973937"}]},"status":"behind","ahead_by":0,"behind_by":1,"total_commits":0,"commits":[],"files":[]}